⚡🇮🇹🇪🇺Following Germany, the Netherlands, and Switzerland, Austria is transferring asylum seekers to Italy under the EU Pact on Migration and Asylum (effective June). Individuals have already been moved by train and bus. 

These "Dubliners" are migrants who enter one EU country and then apply for protection in another. The reform amends the Dublin Regulation, assigning responsibility for processing applications to the country of first entry—in this case, Italy.

